  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Problem Statement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Your startup has a $5,000/month Azure budget but actual spend is $7,200. You need to identify overspending, optimize resource sizing, and implement cost alerts without impacting performance."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "What to Do"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use **Azure Cost Management** to analyze spending patterns. Implement **budgets and alerts** to prevent overruns. Consider **reserved instances** for steady-state workloads and **auto-shutdown** for dev/test resources."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "How to Implement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Azure CLI - Create Budget Alert",
        "language": "bash",
        "code": "az consumption budget create \\\n  --budget-name 'MonthlyBudget' \\\n  --amount 5000 \\\n  --time-grain Monthly \\\n  --start-date 2024-01-01 \\\n  --end-date 2024-12-31 \\\n  --notification-thresholds 80 100 \\\n  --contact-emails 'team@example.com'"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Why Azure Cost Management"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Azure Cost Management is **built-in and free**, integrates with all Azure services, and provides detailed cost analysis by resource, resource group, or tag. Unlike third-party tools, it has direct access to billing data."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "comparison-cards",
      "data": {
        "title": "Cost Management Tools",
        "cards": [
          {
